{"id": "11th_tamil_rev2_q107", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "multiple_choice", "level": "medium", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "11", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "revision_megapack_2", "lesson_id": "rev_u7_u8_sangam_modern_theatre", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "muthukumar_metaphor_clock", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "‘தொலைந்து போனவர்கள்’ கவிதையில் நேரத்தை அளக்கும் கருவியாக அன்றி மனிதனைக் கட்டுப்படுத்தும் எஜமானாக உருவகப்படுத்தப்படுவது எது?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "வாகனம்", "B": "தொலைபேசி", "C": "கடிகாரம்", "D": "நாட்காட்டி"}, "explanation": "மனிதர்கள் கடிகாரத்தின் முட்களுக்குப் பின்னால் ஓடும் இயந்திரப் பொம்மைகளாக மாறிவிட்டதை நா. முத்துக்குமார் இக்கவிதையில் சாடியுள்ளார்."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "In 'Tolainthu Ponavargal', what instrument is personified as a tyrant commanding mechanized human life?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Motor vehicle", "B": "Telephone", "C": "Clock (Gadikaaram)", "D": "Calendar"}, "explanation": "The clock is portrayed as an oppressive master dictating the artificial rhythms of alienated city dwellers."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "C", "accepted_keys": ["C"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "11", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 210, "chapter": null, "section": null, "refer