{"id": "11th_tamil_rev2_q150", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "grammar_identification", "level": "medium", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "11", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "revision_megapack_2", "lesson_id": "rev_u5_u8_grammar_mega_test", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "aakkappeyar_verb_base", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "‘ஓட்டுநர், நடத்துநர், பெறுநர்’ என்பவை எவ்வகை வேர்ச்சொல்லிலிருந்து உருவான ஆக்கப்பெயர்கள்?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "பெயர்-அடி", "B": "வினை-அடி (வினைச்சொல்)", "C": "இடைச்சொல்-அடி", "D": "உரிச்சொல்-அடி"}, "explanation": "ஓட்டு, நடத்து, பெறு என்பவை வினை வேர்கள். இவற்றோடு 'நர்' என்னும் கருத்தாப் பின்னொட்டு இணைந்து வினை-அடி ஆக்கப்பெயர்களாகின்றன."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "From what category of linguistic root base are 'Ottunar', 'Nadathunar', 'Perunar' derived?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Noun stems", "B": "Verb stems (Vinai-adi)", "C": "Particle stems", "D": "Adverbial particle stems"}, "explanation": "Oottu (drive), Nadathu (conduct), Peru (receive) are verbal roots taking the agentive suffix '-Nar'."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "B", "accepted_keys": ["B"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "11", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 191, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "11th Tami