{"id": "11th_tamil_rev2_q160", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "matching", "level": "medium", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "11", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "revision_megapack_2", "lesson_id": "rev_u5_u8_grammar_mega_test", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "architectural_terms_matching", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "கட்டடக் கலைச்சொற்களைப் பொருத்துக:\n(a) Monolithic - 1. ஒற்றைக்கல் கற்றளி\n(b) Corridor - 2. திருச்சுற்று மாளிகை / நடைபாதை\n(c) Pillar - 3. தூண்\n(d) Basement - 4. உபபீடம் / அடித்தளம்", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "a-2, b-1, c-4, d-3", "B": "a-3, b-4, c-1, d-2", "C": "a-4, b-3, c-2, d-1", "D": "a-1, b-2, c-3, d-4"}, "explanation": "Monolithic = ஒற்றைக்கல் கற்றளி (1), Corridor = திருச்சுற்று நடைபாதை (2), Pillar = தூண் (3), Basement = உபபீடம் (4). நேர் பொருத்தம் a-1, b-2, c-3, d-4."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Match archaeological architectural terms with exact Tamil vocabulary:\n(a) Monolithic - 1. Monolithic granite shrine\n(b) Corridor - 2. Cloistered corridor gallery\n(c) Pillar - 3. Pillar / Column\n(d) Basement - 4. Plinth / Basement structure", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "a-2, b-1, c-4, d-3", "B": "a-3, b-4, c-1, d-2", "C": "a-4, b-3, c-2, d-1", "D": "a-1, b-2, c-3, d-4"}, "explanation": "Standard architectural correspondences in Dravidian temple study."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "D", "accepted_keys": ["D"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "boo