{"id": "11th_tamil_rev2_q165", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "grammar_identification", "level": "medium", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "11", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "revision_megapack_2", "lesson_id": "rev_u5_u8_grammar_mega_test", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "aakkappeyar_panpu_anbu", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "‘அன்பன், அறிஞன், கலைஞன்’ ஆகிய சொற்களில் பயின்றுவந்துள்ள ஆக்கப்பெயர்ப் பின்னொட்டுகள் எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "அன், ஞன் (ஆண்பால் கருத்தா பின்னொட்டுகள்)", "B": "அகம்", "C": "இயல்", "D": "மான்"}, "explanation": "அன்பு + அன் = அன்பன்; அறிவு + ஞன் = அறிஞன்; கலை + ஞன் = கலைஞன் என ஆண்பால் மனிதரைக் குறிக்கும் பின்னொட்டுகளால் ஆக்கப்பெயர்களாகின்றன."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Which masculine agentive suffixes form the derivative nouns 'Anban', 'Arinjan', 'Kalainjan'?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "-An, -Njan (masculine agent suffixes)", "B": "-Agam", "C": "-Iyal", "D": "-Maan"}, "explanation": "Suffixes '-An' and '-Njan' productively derive masculine agentive nouns from abstract roots."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "A", "accepted_keys": ["A"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "11", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 191, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "11th Tamil, Unit revision_me